course: dictionary
lesson: 6523
title: Words that can be kind or unkind
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word nerd can be a joke, an insult, or a proud badge. The words around it give you the clues. Ask yourself: who is saying it, and does it sound friendly or cruel?
explain: Jake's mates make a chat called «no nerds allowed» and add Sam by mistake. A rule like that is a put-down, so nerd is being used as a teasing word for someone thought boring or not cool.
explain: Then Sam scrolls up and sees himself called «Professor Sam». The name is meant as a joke at his expense. The word itself does not say unkind, but the clues show the feeling.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. Does "a boring person who studies too much" fit the chat? It does, so you have found the meaning the chat is using.
fact: Nerd is an informal word, so you should use it with care.
fact: Nerd can mean a person who is very interested and clever in one subject, such as computers, science or maths.
fact: Nerd can also be a teasing name for someone thought boring or not cool.
fact: Some people use nerd proudly about themselves, as in «I'm a book nerd».
fact: Nerdy is the adjective, as in «nerdy glasses». Nerds are often clever heroes in stories.
exercise: Jake's mates make a chat called «no nerds allowed». What does nerd mean here? | A person who loves to swim | A person who is cool and popular | A person who is very clever with computers, said proudly | *A person thought of as boring or not cool, said unkindly
exercise: Sam sees himself called «Professor Sam». Why is this probably a teasing name? | It is his birthday name | Professors are always rude | *The chat is mocking him for being clever, so the name is a joke | Sam is a real professor at a university
exercise: Which sentence shows someone is proud to be a nerd? | «Get lost, nerd!» shouted Tom | «No nerds allowed» said the sign on the door | *«I'm a book nerd!» said Priya with a big grin
test: What does «nerdy» describe in «nerdy glasses»? | *Something that looks like a nerd would wear or like | Something that is very wet | Something that is very fast
test: Which phrase means someone who is very interested in computers? | *Computer nerd | Total nerd | Nerdy glasses
exam: Is nerd always an insult? | Yes, but only in stories | Yes, it is always an insult | *No, some people say it proudly about themselves | No, it only means a wise old teacher
